+#
+# Both defects come from the same assumption -- a touchscreen and a GPU -- so
+# the fix is not to patch mpv's options but to drop the second window and the
+# blocking call entirely. This panel now polls the MJPEG snapshot endpoint on a
+# worker thread and paints frames into an ordinary Gtk.Image inside the normal
+# KlipperScreen window. The main loop is never blocked, no foreign window ever
+# takes the input focus, and BackSpace/Escape therefore always leave the panel
